WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.650
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day! {I think this is snappier}{please}

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.520
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.200
Hello. Our show is under way.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:18.080
S4 Presents: It's Our Job to Shine.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.080
As always, we'll be your hosts.
Theater Class, Kisaragi Tsubasa...

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.580
Dance Class, Nikaidou Yuzu! And also...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:29.300
Beauty Class, Kasumi Yozora. And finally...

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:32.220
Song Class, Shiratori Hime.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.180
We are the four glimmering stars, S4!

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.600
Four Star Academy News!

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.440
Yay!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.520
We held our matriculation ceremony just last week.

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.730
Yes, we did!

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:53.860
And yesterday, the new students had their debut concerts.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:58.740
They were all so cute, I could eat them right up.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:02.370
But there was one girl who stood out from all the rest.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:05.080
Nijino Yume-chan!

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.130
She was the sparkliest of them all!

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.840
We'll be keeping a close, close, close eye on Nijino Yume-chan.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.130
What?!

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.340
Th-They're watching me?

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:19.390
That's amazing, Yume-chan.

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.890
Stop it, I don't deserve to be mentioned on a show like this.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.480
That's not true.

00:01:27.190 --> 00:01:30.190
Your performance was outstanding, Yume-chan.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:38.780
Koharu-chan, do you remember being on stage during the concert?

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:43.160
I'll never forget. I was so nervous it all fell to pieces.

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.040
I see. But I...

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:50.920
I don't remember a single thing.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.800
Putting me aside,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.300
there were plenty of others who didn't do well despite being really good.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.680
I'm not really sure, but I guess I was just lucky.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.680
They say that luck's a skill too.

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.690
You think so?

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:09.730
Yeah, must be!

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:14.070
I might've just taken my first real step towards becoming an idol!

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.410
Look, it's Yume-chan!

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.750
You're amazing, Nijino-san.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.120
I saw you on Aikatsu TV!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.080
Th-Thanks...

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:59.010
It seems that everyone here watches Aikatsu TV.{let's have koharu speak in stodgy-english-teacher approved words, sound right?}{sure, yoroshiku}

00:03:59.010 --> 00:03:59.800
Yeah!

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.470
Okay, babies.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.640
Idols are all about stamina.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.510
Every first-year starts with the 
foundation of Aikatsu, running.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.720
Get on it! {this is obviously her thing, but I don't know how to thing it}

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:15.310
Aikatsu! Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.360
That's enough!

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.570
Nijino, just you now.

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:23.360
Okay!

00:04:25.620 --> 00:04:26.990
Louder!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.500
Huh? Why isn't she projecting?

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:30.040
Try again.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:30.830
Okay!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:34.120
She was unbelievable on stage, though.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.710
Use your diaphragm!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.120
Okay!

00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.500
Enough! Everyone take five.

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:41.510
Hey.

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:45.590
Nijino Yume, was it?

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:47.010
Right.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:51.720
Wh-What was that for?

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.940
Hey, can you really call those abs?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.520
Leave me alone.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:59.110
Weren't you that girl with the awesome performance? {wow, english is weird}

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.650
I'm just not seeing it.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.160
The one-week countdown to the class sorting auditions starts now.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.790
You'll start your rockingest class activities this afternoon, babies.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:16.920
Class activities? {so uh, this doesn't exactly sound right. sorting activities?}

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:23.420
You've all been given the privilege of sitting in on whichever class you'd like.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:26.800
Everyone can decide for themselves! Because that's...

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:29.300
Self-producing!

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.810
Come on, Koharu-chan.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:34.100
Let's start with the Wind Dance Class.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.310
Sure!

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.940
You are now cats!

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.940
Let catnip light a fire in your hearts! {so technically this is Silver Vine, which is distinct, but who the hell knows the difference?}{there will always someone who knows the difference}

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:41.980
Meow meow!

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.940
Marvelous, Nikaidou! Be the cat!

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.780
It's no wonder Yuzu-senpai is in S4.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.080
The Phantom of the Cats? {obviously a play on phantom of the opera}{cats is also a musical}

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:57.210
Come on! Let's all dance together!

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:01.210
Worry not! You have it in you!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.090
Bring out more, more, and more of your passion!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:08.090
O-Okay...

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:12.140
The Dance Class felt like being inside a toy box.

00:06:12.140 --> 00:06:13.470
Sure did!

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:17.180
Here's our next stop, the Moon Beauty Class.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:17.980
Yeah!

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:27.860
One, two. One, two.

00:06:29.110 --> 00:06:31.490
Girlies, here for your class activities?

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:32.660
Yes.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.370
Is that so? Then do please sit yourselves thereabouts.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:39.370
You want us to sit on those?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:45.380
Here in the Beauty Class, we are constantly in pursuit of a higher beauty.

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:49.130
There, step with the rhythm!

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.140
One, two! One, two!

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:55.770
This is difficult.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:57.350
But it's kind of fun!

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.270
Wh-Whoa, it's so tall!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.150
Kasumi Yozora-san! {not senpai?}

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.790
Koharu-chan!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.660
Are you okay?

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.580
Yeah...

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.330
Where are my glasses... {my glasses! I can't see anything without my glasses!}

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:22.830
Here you are.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.540
Th-Thank you.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:28.590
You're a lifesaver!

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:32.010
All better now?

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.970
Y-Yes.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.550
That's a relief.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:39.640
I-I'm so sorry for interrupting your lesson.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.810
Goodness! You have such smooth, supple skin.

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:47.440
You must be quite the pure and innocent girl.{in case you were wondering, yes, Yozora is one of 'them'}

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.490
I can tell what kind of person someone is by their skin.{is this what they mean by beauty is skin-deep}

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:56.330
Let's meet again.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:06.210
The Beauty Class was like a jewelry box with all the pretty things in the world in it.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:09.510
What's up?

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:13.720
Yume-chan, I've decided to enter the Beauty Class!

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:18.140
I want to work hard so that Yozora-senpai will compliment me even more!

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.850
What do you think?

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:21.600
Koharu-chan!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:26.860
Do you mind if I stay here and keep sitting in on the Beauty Class?

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:30.110
Not at all! We'll catch up later.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:30.900
Sure.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.490
Now then, this is the Bird Theater Class.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.620
Wow!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:45.620
Okay, stop.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:52.590
Let me think, if I were to liken your acting to something...

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:57.390
Yes, it would be as if I peeled a 
mandarine only to find a banana. {how come I've never seen this word used before? It's not exact, but it's so close}{why is the spelling mandarine}{I feel like I found a distinction between this and mandarin orange before, but it disappeared. oh well}

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:00.890
Don't you get it?

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:05.020
What Yachigusa-sensei is trying to say

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:09.150
is that your acting completely missed her expectations.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:11.900
Okay!

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.400
Kisaragi, demonstrate.

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.150
Right.

00:09:21.740 --> 00:09:25.290
<i>Holy... it's like she suddenly put on a mask.{hmm...}</i>

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:28.630
<i>The room's atmosphere changed in an instant. {everyone's focus is on her/she stole the spotlight}{no, this}</i>

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:37.680
Yes, that is a mandarine.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.430
Distinct from a banana or pineapple.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.640
Okay!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:45.180
<i>So this is the Theater Class.</i>

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:49.060
<i>Okay, time to finish it up with the Flower Song Class!</i>

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.730
<i>You can tell it's the most popular.</i>

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.690
<i>And for some reason, it feels really lighthearted.</i>

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:59.030
<i>Even Hime-senpai is smiling happily.</i>

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:03.790
Are they just going to stay on break?

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.460
When are they going to start their lesson? {Hime too good for sweats}

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.080
Not sure...

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:10.460
Their lesson's long begun.

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.840
Look closely.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.310
It couldn't be!

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:28.350
No way! {these two VAs are so new}

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:32.690
That's exactly it. They're training their abdominals.

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:36.070
And with a smile, no less.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.360
Good, that's enough!

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.950
This is the lesson Shiratori Hime created herself.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.000
We call it the Himetrain! {?}{all aboard}

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.880
Elegant to the eyes, yet terrifying to the core. {oh, like her}

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:54.960
This is the Flower Song Class!

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.210
Well done, ladies.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:00.380
<i>So this is Hime-senpai's Song Class!</i>

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.970
<i>The Song Class has got to be on the top of my list.</i>

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:06.810
Hey!

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.770
You picked the Song Class too?

00:11:10.770 --> 00:11:12.150
Is that a problem?

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:18.110
I have aspirations of being like Hime-senpai.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.990
No matter what you do, you'll never make it into S4.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:26.370
That spot in S4 belongs to me.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:32.920
I'll make it into the Song Class, and join S4 to boot.

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.630
What's with that girl?

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:43.640
So that's what happened.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:47.640
Yeah. I have no idea how to deal with her.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:48.850
Got a second?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:53.270
We're drawing lots. Here.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.560
Lots?

00:11:55.560 --> 00:12:00.530
The academy is going to hold a welcome party for us new students.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:05.530
And we're all supposed to pair up and put on some sort of show.

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.910
It's a yearly tradition.

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.410
And now that you know, good luck.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.040
Bring it on!

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.670
Let's see... I'm number four.

00:12:18.130 --> 00:12:20.800
The other girl in four is... oh!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:21.920
That's her over there.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:33.060
S-Seriously?

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:46.070
Come on, let's just pick one and see how it goes.

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.990
All the upperclassmen are going to be watching, so we need to choose carefully.

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:52.960
You don't need to be so stiff about it.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:55.580
Aren't you the one being too loose?

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.920
We won't know what'll work until we try it out.

00:12:57.920 --> 00:13:00.340
That's all you've been saying this whole time.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:03.840
Looks like we'll never be on the same page.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:07.180
Tell me about it. We're not even in the same book.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:08.600
What's left...

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:11.350
A song...

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:13.350
A song!

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.480
That's it! That's definitely best!

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.490
You can play piano?

00:13:23.900 --> 00:13:27.610
Just for fun. Try singing this note. {"Just for fun" also she then plays a chord}{maybe it's a test to see if hime is mongolian}

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:32.910
What the...

00:13:38.130 --> 00:13:41.000
Hey, are you taking this seriously?

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:47.430
Are you holding back your tremendous skill because you don't want to try?

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:48.390
Not at all...

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:52.600
I always put my heart and soul into singing.

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:55.020
If you're not going to try, then just walk out.

00:13:56.230 --> 00:13:57.640
But I am—

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.360
Practice, then we'll talk.

00:14:00.360 --> 00:14:01.650
Hold it!

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.610
For crying out loud.

00:14:07.400 --> 00:14:08.860
That sounds rough.

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:11.160
She could've been a bit nicer about it.

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:13.490
But you've just got to do it, right?

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.540
I know, but still.

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:16.960
Here, take this.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.420
Sakuraba-san?

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:20.920
What's in that?

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.920
You can use it if you'd like.

00:14:24.800 --> 00:14:26.300
Wait, Sakuraba-san!

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:28.630
Sorry, Yume-chan.

00:14:29.550 --> 00:14:32.930
I need to go practice for my show.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.310
Oh, sure.

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:35.970
Good luck!

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.100
See you later.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:44.940
A score?

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.690
She added all sorts of instructions.{because uh, "notes"}{that doesn't work either}

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:50.450
Did she make this for me?

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.700
Sakuraba-san.

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:03.460
<i>She acts all high and mighty, but she's dedicated to whatever she needs to do.</i>

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.960
<i>I need to work just as hard!</i>

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:18.480
<i>I've gotta start from the foundations so that I can learn to project like Sakuraba-san!</i>

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.520
<i>I won't give up!</i>

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.240
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:43.630
Hey, you've sung the song we're doing on stage before, right?

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:44.330
Yep!

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:48.710
There's a part of the dance I don't get. 
Could you help me out?

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.760
Sure, no problem!

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:55.430
What's after this?

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:58.350
You do this, and then go like this.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.850
I get it now! I feel so much better.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.560
Yeah, that's perfect!

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.610
It's an uplifting song, so I want to have fun with it.

00:16:09.610 --> 00:16:12.700
No arguments here. Let's kill it!

00:16:13.660 --> 00:16:16.910
Oh, how about we both wear our School Dresses too?

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:18.370
Sounds good.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:19.700
Huh?

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.950
What is it?

00:16:21.790 --> 00:16:24.250
Looks like we're finally on the same page.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.420
Now that you mention it, we are.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:35.890
Today, we hold the welcome party for our new students.

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:39.010
Let's make this an enjoyable experience for all.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:45.020
Four Star Academy hosts such extravagant parties.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.020
It's amazing!

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:49.320
Hey, party people!

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:54.360
It's time for our yearly tradition, the fun-filled stage performances from our newbies!

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:57.280
It's showtime!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.170
It's finally our turn.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.010
Let's sing our hearts out!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:15.840
Yeah!

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.890
That Nijino Yume girl wasn't anything special.

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:56.060
Yeah, even though she had a pretty good performance the last time.

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.860
I guess she didn't take it seriously.{ever since wixoss this word has been messing with me}

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.690
Hey, mind keeping your presumptions to yourselves?

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:07.950
She took this seriously. I could tell from singing with her.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:12.000
Some have the latent gift of song.

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:15.330
If you waste your time giggling and gossiping, you'll be passed in no time.

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:22.840
Um... thank you.

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:26.590
No need. I just said the truth.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:32.470
And just so you know, no matter how good you get, you'll never make it into S4.

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.230
What?!

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.230
That spot in S4 belongs to me.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:41.610
It's my dream to join S4 too!

00:21:41.610 --> 00:21:45.610
Now you're talking. You're my number one rival,{so someone always has to be the 1-gou something in aikatsu}

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.110
Yume.

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:49.990
The same goes for you,

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.410
Rola!

00:21:56.830 --> 00:22:01.920
It appears that there was quite the gap between today and her previous performance.

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:05.970
It appears that some sort of special phenomenon occurred last time.

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:08.760
Was that her true skill,

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:11.720
or simply a coincidence?

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:19.770
Whatever the case may be, should I judge her to be unfit for Four Star Academy,

